<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rand Revolt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1922">1922</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/witwatersrand">The Rand</a> Revolt was an armed uprising of white mineworkers on the Witwatersrand in 1922, sparked by mine owners' plans to cut costs by employing more black workers in semi-skilled jobs. Strikers organised in commandos seized parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannesburg">Johannesburg</a> in March, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-smuts">Jan Smuts</a>'s government declared martial law and crushed the revolt with troops, artillery and aircraft; more than 150 people died. Its political cost helped bring Hertzog's Pact government to power in 1924.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rand-revolt.jpg" alt="Rand Revolt" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agence Rol · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rand_Rebellion.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
